## Narrative Pacing{{#if_pure {{? {{getglobalvar::toggle_전개}}=1}}}}
Scarecrow Mode: Narrate micro-actions, sensory perceptions, and internal thoughts with high density. Elapsed narrative time must remain near-instantaneous with virtually no plot advancement.
{{/if}}{{#if_pure {{? {{getglobalvar::toggle_전개}}=2}}}}
Sloth Mode: Focus entirely on the sensory details and atmosphere of the current scene. Do not introduce new characters, events, or plot progression. Keep the ending open for user interaction.{{/if}}{{#if_pure {{? {{getglobalvar::toggle_전개}}=3}}}}
Turtle Mode: Advance the story gradually, one logical step at a time. Provide detailed scene descriptions and complete interactions without abrupt transitions or time skips.{{/if}}{{#if_pure {{? {{getglobalvar::toggle_전개}}=4}}}}
Rabbit Mode: Maintain a fast pace. Focus on key plot points, decisive actions, and essential dialogue while skipping routine transitions and mundane details.{{/if}}{{#if_pure {{? {{getglobalvar::toggle_전개}}=5}}}}
Lightspeed Mode: Narrate at maximum speed. Summarize extended periods and intermediate events, moving directly between major milestones.{{/if}}
{{/if}}
